{
  "title": "One Loose Wire: Why the Key Bridge Fell",
  "slug": "key-bridge-collapse",
  "audio": "audio/voiceover.mp3",
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "b01",
      "chapter": "Cold open",
      "narration": "At 1:25 in the morning on March 26th, 2024, a loaded containership leaving Baltimore lost its electrical power.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "stamp",
          "text": "1:25 AM",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-night-industrial-shore-reflections"
          ],
          "subtext": "March 26, 2024"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-night-container-terminal-aerial"
          ],
          "at": "a loaded containership"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-bulb-flickers-out"
          ],
          "at": "lost its electrical power."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b02",
      "narration": "The Dali was 984 feet long, and about 3,200 feet from the Francis Scott Key Bridge.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-night-ship-hull-side"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "route",
          "keyframes": [
            {
              "clock": "1:25:00",
              "feet": 3200,
              "note": "3.3 ship lengths"
            },
            {
              "clock": "1:25:00",
              "feet": 3200,
              "note": "Power lost"
            }
          ],
          "at": "about 3,200 feet"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b03",
      "narration": "Within eight seconds, its engine had shut down, and its steering pumps had no power. The ship kept moving.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-er-diesel-cylinder-heads"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-er-pump-motors-tank"
          ],
          "at": "its steering pumps"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-tug-night-vision2"
          ],
          "at": "The ship kept moving."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b04",
      "narration": "Four minutes and nine seconds later, it struck a pier of the bridge. Thirteen seconds after that, the pier gave way, and the central spans fell.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "uscg-dawn-truss-silhouette"
          ],
          "label": "Dawn, March 26, 2024 · U.S. Coast Guard"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "ntsb-aerial-pier-stub-truss"
          ],
          "label": "NTSB drone",
          "at": "the pier gave way,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b05",
      "narration": "Six men from a road crew working on the bridge were killed.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "footage",
        "assets": [
          "ntsb-aerial-severed-roadway"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b06",
      "narration": "The cause had been on board since the ship was built. It was small enough to hold between two fingers.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-ship-no-smoking-stencil"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "evidence",
          "heading": "Exhibit A",
          "items": [
            {
              "asset": "mir-fig51-terminal-block-381-wire1",
              "note": "Small enough to hold"
            }
          ],
          "at": "It was small enough"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b07",
      "narration": "How does a ship that size lose everything at once? And why did a 47-year-old bridge come down in seconds?",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-night-ship-at-pier-lights"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-bridge-lights-river-night"
          ],
          "at": "And why did"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b08",
      "chapter": "The world before",
      "narration": "The Francis Scott Key Bridge opened in 1977, carrying Maryland 695 across the mouth of Baltimore's harbor. It belonged to the Maryland Transportation Authority, the MDTA.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-harbor-bridge-aerial"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "map-collision-location"
          ],
          "label": "Baltimore, Maryland",
          "at": "across the mouth"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-cg-boat-baltimore-skyline"
          ],
          "at": "It belonged to"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b09",
      "narration": "It was a steel through-truss about 9,086 feet long, 185 feet above the shipping channel. In 2023, it carried 34,121 vehicles a day.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-barge-truss-bridge-dawn"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-tug-barge-under-spans"
          ],
          "at": "185 feet above"
        },
        {
          "kind": "stamp",
          "text": "34,121",
          "assets": [
            "broll-highway-topdown-day"
          ],
          "subtext": "Vehicles a day, 2023",
          "at": "In 2023,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b10",
      "narration": "Ships passed between Piers 17 and 18. From the edge of the 700-foot channel to either pier was only 200 feet.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-tug-bow-under-bridge"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-harbor-tug-wake-aerial"
          ],
          "at": "From the edge"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b11",
      "narration": "The Dali was Singapore-flagged, built in 2015 by HD Hyundai Heavy Industries, and managed by Synergy Marine.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "refloat-transit-tugs"
          ],
          "label": "The Dali, May 2024 · USACE"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-container-stacks-topdown"
          ],
          "at": "built in 2015"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-ship-hull-under-cranes"
          ],
          "at": "managed by Synergy Marine."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b12",
      "narration": "It had one main engine and one rudder. Its steering, the engine's cooling-water pumps and most of its lights ran on generator power.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "mir-fig04-dali-helm"
          ],
          "label": "The Dali's helm · NTSB"
        },
        {
          "kind": "power",
          "steps": [
            {
              "clock": "12:36 AM",
              "label": "Underway on generators 3 and 4",
              "on": [
                "DG3",
                "DG4",
                "HV",
                "ME",
                "TR",
                "LV",
                "STEER",
                "COOL",
                "FUEL",
                "LIGHTS"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "at": "Its steering,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b13",
      "narration": "On the bridge that night, a Brawner Builders crew was filling potholes. An inspector walked the span, checking on drying cement.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-night-highway-valley"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-night-bokeh-fence"
          ],
          "at": "An inspector walked"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b14",
      "chapter": "The day of",
      "narration": "The afternoon before, the Dali blacked out twice at the dock.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "stamp",
        "text": "March 25",
        "assets": [
          "broll-ship-alongside-cranes"
        ],
        "subtext": "2:20 PM"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b15",
      "narration": "A crewmember closed a generator's exhaust damper by mistake. Minutes later, a pump feeding fuel to another generator was not restarted in time.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-er-overhead-work"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "stamp",
          "text": "2:27 PM",
          "assets": [
            "broll-er-purifiers-piping"
          ],
          "subtext": "Second blackout",
          "at": "Minutes later,"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-er-boots-deckplate"
          ],
          "at": "was not restarted"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b16",
      "narration": "Afterward, the electrician switched to a transformer, and a breaker called HR1, that had not been used in at least seven months.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-substation-insulators"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-breaker-hands-screwdriver"
          ],
          "at": "and a breaker called HR1,"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-clock-hands-timelapse"
          ],
          "at": "that had not been used"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b17",
      "narration": "Just after midnight, two pilots boarded. At about 12:36 the Dali got underway. By 1:08 its tugs had been released, as is normal in Baltimore.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-night-pier-lights"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "stamp",
          "text": "12:36 AM",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-night-harbor-reflections-teal"
          ],
          "subtext": "Underway",
          "at": "At about 12:36"
        },
        {
          "kind": "stamp",
          "text": "1:08 AM",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-night-water-glitter"
          ],
          "subtext": "Tugs released",
          "at": "By 1:08"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b18",
      "narration": "At 1:25, a breaker opened with no alarm. The ship's low-voltage power went dark.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "stamp",
          "text": "1:25:00 AM",
          "assets": [
            "ecdis-playback-final-track"
          ],
          "subtext": "First blackout"
        },
        {
          "kind": "power",
          "steps": [
            {
              "clock": "1:24:59",
              "label": "Underway",
              "on": [
                "DG3",
                "DG4",
                "HV",
                "ME",
