      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b39",
      "narration": "The flushing pump explained the second blackout. A January email from the previous chief engineer had described the arrangement. But it did not explain the first.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "mir-fig13-plant-0127-04"
          ],
          "label": "Power at 1:27:04 · NTSB"
        },
        {
          "kind": "document",
          "source": "NTSB MIR-25-40, p. 94 (January 2024 email)",
          "quote": "not in use all pumps heaters etc isolated after piping modification and permanently kept on LSMGO [flushing pump] line.",
          "highlight": "permanently kept on LSMGO [flushing pump] line",
          "at": "A January email"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b40",
      "narration": "The first began when breaker HR1 opened on its own, with no alarm. It was as if an operator had turned the switch.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-breaker-test-set-panel"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-old-control-room"
          ],
          "at": "It was as if"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b41",
      "narration": "On April 29th, during testing, HR1 tripped again. Shipyard engineers traced it to a single wire: Wire 1, in Terminal Block 381.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "stamp",
          "text": "April 29, 2024",
          "assets": [
            "broll-breaker-test-cables"
          ],
          "subtext": "HR1 trips again"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
