          ],
          "at": "Under the microscope,"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "mir-fig58-wire1-ferrule-gouges"
          ],
          "label": "Wire 1 ferrule · NTSB",
          "at": "the wire's metal tip,"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "mir-fig62-arcing-damage-gate-face"
          ],
          "label": "Arcing damage · NTSB",
          "at": "and on the clamp"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b44",
      "chapter": "The cause",
      "narration": "To understand the wire, go back to 2015, when the Dali was built.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "stamp",
        "text": "2015",
        "assets": [
          "broll-night-hook-in-hold"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b45",
      "narration": "Each control wire got a heat-shrunk label band printed with its terminal number. The builder told the NTSB it had no specific materials, instructions or training for installing the switchboards.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-hands-screwdriver-terminal-blocks"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "mir-fig42-hv-lv-switchboards"
          ],
          "label": "The Dali's switchboards · NTSB",
          "at": "The builder told"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b46",
      "narration": "On Wire 1, the band was slid too far down. It covered the ferrule's blue collar, so the wire could not be fully inserted.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "document",
        "source": "NTSB MIR-25-40, p. xiii",
        "quote": "Wire 1’s label band (wire-label banding) covered all of the ferrule’s blue insulated collar, increasing the ferrule’s overall circumference, preventing the wire from being fully inserted into its terminal block",
        "highlight": "preventing the wire from being fully inserted"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b47",
      "narration": "Done correctly, the band sits above the collar and the ferrule seats fully in the spring clamp. On Wire 1, its tip rested on the clamp's gate.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "evidence",
        "heading": "Same wire, two ways",
        "items": [
          {
            "asset": "banding-correct-installation",
            "note": "Correct: band above collar"
          },
          {
            "asset": "banding-wire1-installation",
            "note": "Wire 1: band over collar"
          }
        ],
        "links": [
          [
            0,
            1
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b48",
      "narration": "That left an intermittent contact. Nobody noticed, partly because the breaker it served had sat unused for months.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "mir-fig64-arcing-gap-diagram"
          ],
          "label": "NTSB illustration, not to scale"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-electrician-at-cabinet"
          ],
          "at": "Nobody noticed,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b49",
      "narration": "The last switchboard inspection, three days before the accident, found no abnormalities. Infrared thermal imaging, the NTSB found, may have caught the loose wire.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "prelim-fig08-investigator-hv-switchboard"
          ],
          "label": "NTSB investigator at the switchboard, after the accident"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-er-gauge-panel"
          ],
          "at": "Infrared thermal imaging,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b50",
      "narration": "So, at or just before 1:25, the wire let go. HR1 opened. The cooling-water pump stopped, the engine shut down, and the steering died.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "power",
        "steps": [
          {
            "clock": "1:24:59",
            "label": "Wire 1 still making contact",
            "on": [
              "DG3",
