    {
      "id": "b62",
      "chapter": "Aftermath",
      "narration": "On May 13th, explosive charges cut the fallen truss off the Dali's bow. On May 20th, the ship was refloated.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "stamp",
          "text": "May 13, 2024",
          "assets": [
            "demolition-side-view-uscg"
          ],
          "subtext": "Controlled demolition"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "demolition-blast-closeup"
          ],
          "at": "cut the fallen truss"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "refloat-timelapse"
          ],
          "label": "May 20, 2024 · USACE",
          "at": "On May 20th,"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b63",
      "narration": "About 50,000 tons of material came out of the river. The Fort McHenry Channel fully reopened on June 10th.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-final-segment-lift"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "channel-reopened-ship-passes-piers"
          ],
          "label": "Fort McHenry Channel, June 2024",
          "at": "The Fort McHenry Channel"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b64",
      "narration": "The Dali was repaired in China, and returned to service in January 2025.",
      "visual": {
        "kind": "footage",
        "assets": [
          "refloat-damaged-bow-terminal"
        ],
        "label": "The Dali's bow, May 2024"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b65",
      "narration": "In March 2025, the NTSB issued urgent recommendations: 30 owners of 68 bridges in 19 states should calculate the same collapse risk.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "stamp",
          "text": "March 2025",
          "assets": [
            "wreck-site-after-refloat"
          ],
          "subtext": "Urgent recommendations"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-tug-under-bridge"
          ],
          "at": "30 owners of 68 bridges"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b66",
      "narration": "The final report asked for more, from a fix to the shipyard's banding procedure to ways of warning drivers and workers on bridges.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-container-inspectors"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-highway-traffic-aerial-day"
          ],
          "at": "to ways of warning drivers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b67",
      "narration": "The NTSB found that the quick actions of the pilots, the dispatcher and the MDTA police prevented a greater loss of life.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-bridge-wing-mariners"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-dispatcher-keyboard"
          ],
          "at": "the dispatcher"
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-police-cruiser-approaching"
          ],
          "at": "and the MDTA police"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b68",
      "narration": "Six men still died: Alejandro Hernández Fuentes, Dorlian Ronial Castillo Cabrera, Maynor Yassir Suazo Sandoval, Miguel Ángel Luna González, and two of their co-workers.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "kind": "footage",
          "assets": [
            "broll-px-memorial-candles-night"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "footage",
